Any person may be licensed under this Article if they do the following:
(1) Complete a training course approved by Macon-Bibb County, which covers, at a minimum, the following subjects:
a. Responsible sales and service of alcoholic beverages;
b. Identifying false or counterfeit ID cards;
c. State and local laws governing the sales and service of alcohol beverages; and
d. Criminal and civil liabilities and other consequences for violations of alcoholic beverage laws or ordinances, or for selling or serving alcoholic beverages irresponsibly;
(2) Complete a license application, including:
a. The applicant's name, home address, mailing address, telephone number, email address, Social Security number, date of birth, and any other information deemed necessary by Macon-Bibb County;
b. Proof of the applicant's identity;
c. Proof of successful completion of the requirements set forth in subsections (1) and (2) of this Section;
d. SAVE verification through the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services component of the United States Department of Homeland Security;
e. A current photograph of the applicant; and
f. A notarized sworn statement attesting to the accuracy and completeness of all information submitted.
(3) Pay an annual license fee.
(4) Applicants for an Alcohol Handler's license shall not be required to pay the application fee provided for in Subsection 4-23(b).
(Ord. No. O-18-0109, § 1, 12-4-2018)

1210:
